Export {{ model }} to an OpenVINO IR directory at {{ out }}, loadable by optimum-intel's
OVModelForCausalLM, with {{ fmt }} weights. Download what you need (unset HF_HUB_OFFLINE for
it).

First run `{{ python }} -I {{ preflight }} {{ model }}`; it prints JSON and exits with:
0 exportable; 4 no optimum-intel export config for the model_type (or no transformers
integration at all); 5 supported, but the installed transformers is outside the config's
range (`transformers.pin` is the pin); 6 the installed transformers is too old to know the
model_type (`minimum_transformers`); 7 the Hub repo is gated, private or missing. For 5 and
6 make the pinned transformers part of the layered venv, and use that same version for the
export and for the final load check: tokenizer files are version-specific. For 4 and 7 write
{"error": ...} with the preflight's `next_step` -- do not patch optimum-intel, and never look
for, print or log a Hub token. `extra_pip_deps` lists what the family needs besides
optimum-intel[openvino]. A model that is not a text-generating decoder (a VLM, ASR,
diffusion) cannot be captured: write {"error": ...}.

Export with `optimum-cli export openvino -m {{ model }} --weight-format {{ fmt }} <tmp>`:
 - a node-local TMPDIR and output directory, then copy to {{ out }}: temp files on NFS
   break the export (`.nfs...` FileNotFoundError at the end);
 - "Maximum required is X, got: Y" after tracing starts is an upper transformers cap:
   pin transformers<=X (with transformers 5.0 also huggingface-hub>=1.3,<2 and
   datasets>=4,<5) and export again;
 - some ids (Qwen3-1.7B/4B/8B, ...) have data-aware quantization defaults for int4/int8
   that need the `datasets` package;
 - `--trust-remote-code` only after reading the model's code; a hub 504 is worth a retry;
 - the weights must fit the device: if the export is too large for it, say so in the error.

Check that, under the framework's interpreter,
OVModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained("{{ out }}", device="GPU") loads it and generates 4 tokens.
Write prepared.json {"model": "{{ out }}", "transformers": "<version used>"}, or
{"error": "<why>", "stage": "preflight|export|load", "next_step": "<what a person would do>"}.
